    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0327" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg307"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extracts.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Pike to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 120.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">The Hague,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>The war clouds thicken. England seems disposed to side with Austria and Prussia
                    on the German and Danish question, while France appears to aim to <pb
                        facs="0328" n="308" xml:id="pg308"/> make friends of the smaller German
                    powers, who do not at all agree with the two dominant states of the German
                    Confederation.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>A new minister to take the place of Mr. Van der Maeson has not yet been
                    found.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES S. PIKE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c., &amp;c.,
                        &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
